        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: live updater survives launchd teardown and retargets wrapped gateways",
        "body": "Closes #104945\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators updating a source-backed macOS Gateway could be left with a stopped service or malformed LaunchAgent when launchd teardown was still in progress or the service used a generated environment wrapper.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe updater now retries its fail-closed native stopped-state proof for a bounded ten-second window after `launchctl bootout`, accepting a stop-command error only when the job and listener are conclusively gone. It also replaces the verified `ProgramArguments` array as one plist value, avoiding `plutil` array-index insertion while preserving every other service argument and environment value.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSource-backed macOS Gateways can update through transient launchd teardown without an unnecessary recovery failure, and wrapped LaunchAgents are retargeted without duplicate entrypoints. No release or version change is included.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Live clawmac reproduction: the old updater failed immediately after `launchctl bootout` while the job/listener were still disappearing.\n- Live plist reproduction: `plutil -replace ProgramArguments.<index>` produced both the source and snapshot entrypoints in the wrapper-backed LaunchAgent.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/openclaw-live-updater.test.ts` — 47 passed.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` — passed.\n- Fresh structured autoreview after the current-main rebase — no accepted/actionable findings.\n- AI-assisted; implementation and proof reviewed by the maintainer agent.\n",
